workedExamples.question_text:
Name the two sides involved, choose the trigonometric ratio, then find $x$ correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (4,0);\coordinate (C) at (4,2.4995);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw (3.75,0)--(3.75,0.25)--(4,0.25);
\draw (0.65,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=32,radius=0.65];
\path (0.95,0.27) node {$32^{\circ}$};
\path (4,1.25) node[right] {$x$};
\path (2,1.25) node[above left] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
$x$ is opposite the marked angle; $10$ cm is the hypotenuse. Use sine.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (4,0);\coordinate (C) at (4,2.4995);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw (3.75,0)--(3.75,0.25)--(4,0.25);
\draw (0.65,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=32,radius=0.65];
\path (0.95,0.27) node {$32^{\circ}$};
\path (4,1.25) node[right] {$x\ (O)$};
\path (2,1.25) node[above left] {$10\text{ cm}\ (H)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*}\sin\theta&=\frac{O}{H}\\\sin32^{\circ}&=\frac{x}{10}\\10\sin32^{\circ}&=x\\x&\approx5.30\text{ cm}\end{align*}$

workedExamples.question_text:
An $18$ m ladder leans against a vertical wall at $40^{\circ}$ to the level ground. Find the distance $x$ from the foot of the ladder to the wall, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (4,0);\coordinate (C) at (4,3.3564);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw (3.75,0)--(3.75,0.25)--(4,0.25);
\draw (0.65,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=40,radius=0.65];
\path (0.95,0.35) node {$40^{\circ}$};
\path (2,0) node[below] {$x$};
\path (2,1.6782) node[above left] {$18\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
$x$ is adjacent to the marked angle; the ladder is the hypotenuse. Use cosine.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (4,0);\coordinate (C) at (4,3.3564);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw (3.75,0)--(3.75,0.25)--(4,0.25);
\draw (0.65,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=40,radius=0.65];
\path (0.95,0.35) node {$40^{\circ}$};
\path (2,0) node[below] {$x\ (A)$};
\path (2,1.6782) node[above left] {$18\text{ m}\ (H)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*}\cos\theta&=\frac{A}{H}\\\cos40^{\circ}&=\frac{x}{18}\\18\cos40^{\circ}&=x\\x&\approx13.79\text{ m}\end{align*}$

workedExamples.question_text:
A roof rafter rises at $35^{\circ}$ over a horizontal run of $7$ m. Find its vertical rise $x$, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (4,0);\coordinate (C) at (4,2.8008);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw (3.75,0)--(3.75,0.25)--(4,0.25);
\draw (0.65,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=35,radius=0.65];
\path (0.95,0.30) node {$35^{\circ}$};
\path (2,0) node[below] {$7\text{ m}$};
\path (4,1.4004) node[right] {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
$x$ is opposite the marked angle; $7$ m is adjacent. Use tangent.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (4,0);\coordinate (C) at (4,2.8008);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw (3.75,0)--(3.75,0.25)--(4,0.25);
\draw (0.65,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=35,radius=0.65];
\path (0.95,0.30) node {$35^{\circ}$};
\path (2,0) node[below] {$7\text{ m}\ (A)$};
\path (4,1.4004) node[right] {$x\ (O)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*}\tan\theta&=\frac{O}{A}\\\tan35^{\circ}&=\frac{x}{7}\\7\tan35^{\circ}&=x\\x&\approx4.90\text{ m}\end{align*}$

workedExamples.question_text:
The marked angle is at the top of this right-angled triangle. Find $x$ correct to $1$ decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,4);\coordinate (B) at (0,0);\coordinate (C) at (2.8008,0);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw (0,0.25)--(0.25,0.25)--(0.25,0);
\draw (0,3.35) arc[start angle=270,end angle=305,radius=0.65];
\path (0.30,3.03) node {$35^{\circ}$};
\path (1.4004,0) node[below] {$x$};
\path (1.4004,2) node[above right] {$16\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
Measure the side names from the top angle: $x$ is opposite and $16$ m is the hypotenuse.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,4);\coordinate (B) at (0,0);\coordinate (C) at (2.8008,0);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw (0,0.25)--(0.25,0.25)--(0.25,0);
\draw (0,3.35) arc[start angle=270,end angle=305,radius=0.65];
\path (0.30,3.03) node {$35^{\circ}$};
\path (1.4004,0) node[below] {$x\ (O)$};
\path (1.4004,2) node[above right] {$16\text{ m}\ (H)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*}\sin\theta&=\frac{O}{H}\\\sin35^{\circ}&=\frac{x}{16}\\16\sin35^{\circ}&=x\\x&\approx9.2\text{ m}\end{align*}$

workedExamples.question_text:
Find $x$ correct to $2$ decimal places. The angle is given in degrees and minutes.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (4,0);\coordinate (C) at (4,2.5483);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw (3.75,0)--(3.75,0.25)--(4,0.25);
\draw (0.75,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=32.5,radius=0.75];
\path (1.28,0.35) node {$32^{\circ}30'$};
\path (4,1.2742) node[right] {$x$};
\path (2,1.2742) node[above left] {$12\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
$x$ is opposite the marked angle; $12$ cm is the hypotenuse. Enter $32^{\circ}30'$ using the calculator's DMS input, or use $32+\frac{30}{60}=32.5^{\circ}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (4,0);\coordinate (C) at (4,2.5483);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw (3.75,0)--(3.75,0.25)--(4,0.25);
\draw (0.75,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=32.5,radius=0.75];
\path (1.28,0.35) node {$32^{\circ}30'$};
\path (4,1.2742) node[right] {$x\ (O)$};
\path (2,1.2742) node[above left] {$12\text{ cm}\ (H)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*}\sin\theta&=\frac{O}{H}\\\sin(32^{\circ}30')&=\frac{x}{12}\\12\sin(32^{\circ}30')&=x\\x&\approx6.45\text{ cm}\end{align*}$
